        <mxCell id="sjAGbNYinLBW1bgxu3tC-65" value="360 degree model that can be exploded.&lt;div&gt;Gestures:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- double click/tap - explode/implode item under cursor&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- mouse wheel or pinch - zoom in/out&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;In Simulation Mode, clicking on a key will depress the key and higlight:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- mechanical motion - orange border around moving parts&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- electrical connectivity - electric blue moiving arrows with speed controls at bottom of page.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Moving the mouse around the parts will show info blocks for the current state of the part (hint box style)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;NOTE: Models likely in STL format (if this is possible to use?) this is sort of like what most CAD aplications would do to build multiple parts into an assembly.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
